cord runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair came in at 47% of normal on the middle of the grids, while May to June ran 168%. Grid 25112 had its driest year in 1965 at 67% of normal. On grid 25113, the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 sits at 134.5, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
